# Synchronization

## Purpose

> **Scope:** Fetching and reconciling the collection and every member submodule
> **Key items:** fetch first, report state, fast-forward, pin reconciliation,
> push order

Follow it when the request asks to synchronize, merge remotes, or update the
collection and its members.

## Procedure

1. Fetch every remote - the collection and each member. Report any fetch failure
   and continue with what succeeded.
2. Report each repository's state: clean or dirty, ahead/behind its upstream,
   detached HEAD, submodule pin status (`-` unfetched, `+` moved off pin).
3. Fast-forward the collection, then each member whose state allows it. A dirty,
   diverged, or detached member is reported, never force-merged.
4. Reconcile pins: a member that moved ahead of its recorded pin is re-pinned in
   the collection only after its commit exists on the member's remote.
5. Push members before the collection, only on explicit approval - synchronization
   never commits or pushes on its own.

## Boundaries

- Fetch is the only ungated network action - everything that writes to a remote
  waits for approval.
- Report what was fetched, merged, pinned, pushed, and skipped - a skipped member
  names its blocking state.
